# the-odds-api.com - powers GET /events and GET /events/:id (fixtures and
# odds). Billed by request cost (markets x regions), reported via response
# headers - see src/providers/the-odds-api/client.ts's logQuota. Accepts a
# comma-separated list of keys - if the first one fails (quota exhausted,
# revoked, ...) the client automatically tries the next, only erroring once
# every key has failed. e.g. THE_ODDS_API_KEY=key1,key2,key3
THE_ODDS_API_KEY=
# api-sports.io (football) - powers GET /events/:id/live for currently-live
# matches: scoreboard, key events (goals/cards/subs), and stats. Free tier
# is 100 requests/day - see the poll-interval comment in
# src/providers/api-sports/live-tracker-service.ts for the budget math.
API_SPORTS_KEY=
# therundown.io - a second, not-yet-wired-in odds/scores provider (see
# src/providers/therundown/client.ts). Auth via the X-Therundown-Key header.
# Not read by server.ts yet - the client exists and is tested, but nothing
# in the app calls it. Set this only when actually plugging it in.
THERUNDOWN_API_KEY=
